-## Implementation notes (2026-10-21, fourth batch)
+## Phase 18 - Sixth-batch user QA findings (Pixel 3a AVD) [ ]
+
+Five new findings from the user's on-device pass, plus the ratified
+sixth-batch decisions (2026-10-21). Answered inline below; fixes are
+the next work batch.
+
+- [ ] 18.1 Number/pin keyboard labels off-center: digits sit right of
+      center and hint letters START at the digit position and run
+      right, overlapping. Root cause (source): KeyboardView.KitKat
+      ported sizes/colors but NOT the donor label-alignment geometry -
+      the modern KeyDrawParams consumes keyLabelHorizontalPadding /
+      hint off-center ratios that the donor KeyboardView.KLP set
+      differently, and on kbd_number/kbd_phone layouts the modern
+      defaults shift text. Fix: port the donor alignment paddings +
+      hint-label placement semantics into themes-kitkat.xml.
+- [ ] 18.2 Back arrow rotates while the IME is open (modern navbar
+      IME-visibility behavior: back glyph rotates 180). 4.4 NEVER
+      rotated glyphs - the back arrow pointed left, always. Fix:
+      suppress the navbar IME-rotation in 3-button mode (the KitKat
+      navbar is 3-button-only on this build anyway).
+- [?] 18.3 Shade footer "Manage"/"History" buttons: verified these
+      are 12.2 leftovers (header X covers clear-all; footer buttons
+      are a modern surface the donor did not have). OPEN QUESTION
+      (user): drop the footer rows entirely for donor fidelity?
+- [ ] 18.4 Expanded-QS gap between header and brightness bar: NOT
+      donor geometry - the 4.4 QS panel had the slider immediately
+      under the 48dp header. The 12.1 margin zeroing covered the
+      half-open state only; the expanded-panel container margins
+      (qqs_layout_* / stack padding) survive. Fix: apply the same
+      margin zeroing to the expanded QS container.
+- [ ] 18.5 Shade-open transition fades like modern (window alpha),
+      not the 4.4 opaque PanelView height ride with grab handle.
+      SCOPE WARNING: touches ScrimController/ShadeController window
+      animation paths, which couple to the keyguard window (the
+      hard-constraint area). 15.2 fixed the fling physics; this is
+      the open-animation half. Needs a careful spike.
+
+## Phase 16 ratifications + P19 environment (user decisions, 2026-10-21)
+
+- DeskClock: port VERBATIM (no modern sounds/settings UX). Theme:
+  faithful to the 4.4 actual theme choice (Holo Light + dark action
+  bar era semantics - NOT blanket dark). SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM
+  manifest perm + shim approved.
+- Messaging: DEFERRED ENTIRELY - no port, ship modern, the app
+  cannot be tested without a SIM. Tier 1 remainder is DeskClock only.
+- 4.4 reference build (P19): second repo workspace at ~/kitkat-build
+  (OUTSIDE ~/android/lineage, never in the ROM repos),
+  android-4.4.4_r1, sdk_phone_x86_64 emulator target; disk space
+  approved; full emulator build; needs the 4.4-era JDK toolchain.
+- 4.4-native KitKatWidgetPlayground variant to build INTO the 4.4
+  ROM (API-19 resource syntax); written pixel-diff report per
+  widget family (accept-and-document deltas).
+- Playback verification scope (user AVD): just confirm playback
+  works (Music + DeskClock alarms).
+- All touch/hardware-only items (14.11 marquee, 15.2 fling feel,
+  14.1 glow, gesture typing): DOCUMENT-DEFERRED, not open blockers.
 
